From 6dbe95980280750106d4e452df6d97a6d847b2b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:41:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ggml: TurboQuant TQ3_1S/TQ4_1S weight formats behind
 GGML_ARIFI_TURBO_WEIGHT_QUANTS

Closes the 'TurboQuant weight quants' merge slot. Type-ids 45/46 adopted VERBATIM per
docs/TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md 3.1 - both were free in our fork and upstream, so their files
load natively with no gate, no retag. The blocking 'collision' the slot was parked on does
not exist for serialized types; only the KV runtime ids overlap, and those are NOT ported.

Only the weight half of the source file is taken. The KV-cache turbo codecs from the same
file stay out: measured a loss on this hardware (plain q4_0 KV is smaller AND faster,
lane-110C) and they are runtime-only types belonging in the 200+ block.

Weight formats are self-contained where the KV codec was not - dequantize applies the
inverse randomized Hadamard transform itself, so no graph-level rotation op is required.

Gate is a CMake option, not an env var, for the same reason as GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFPX_FORMATS:
vec_dot is bound at LINK time from type_traits_cpu[] (LL-250). Enum ids and ftypes stay
unconditional (ABI); only implementations are gated. Default OFF, on measurement.

DEVIATION FROM SOURCE, deliberate: the upstream vec_dot calls malloc() TWICE PER CALL for
whole-row scratch. vec_dot is the innermost hot path, so that is a defect rather than a
design. Both formats dequantize block-locally, so a fixed stack buffer replaces it and the
allocation disappears. Numerically identical - same to_float kernels, same values.

Dispatch trap handled the way the ROCmFP slot proved: 7 type-id switch sites in ops.cpp
carry default: and got gated cases (the silent class that aborted this port at runtime on
get_rows); the exhaustive clamp switch has no default: and gets UNCONDITIONAL cases, or the
OFF build emits -Wswitch. Both arms now build warning-free.

Taken-from: llama-cpp-turboquant@c26cbdffc (ggml/src/ggml-turbo-quant.c, weight half)
Origin: ArifiLabs lane-110D, merge-slot 'TurboQuant weight quants'
Measured-effect: PROVEN end-to-end on this estate - our llama-quantize produced a TQ4_1S
0.5B from fp16 and our llama-server served it coherently (' Paris. It is the capital of the
country of France.'). Head-to-head vs plain Q4_0 from the SAME source, same binary, same
harness: TQ4_1S 438.3 MiB @ 4.47/4.47 t/s decode vs Q4_0 408.9 MiB @ 49.30/49.73 t/s -
BIGGER and ~11x SLOWER on the CPU path, because no SIMD kernel exists for it and the format
is a 5.0 bpw operating point against Q4_0's 4.5. Confirms default OFF on our own numbers
rather than an inherited claim. Contended box (sibling lane running): indicative, a clean
re-bench is owed before any published figure. Quality NOT assessed (n=1).
